mongoose
------------------------------------------
Mongoose is the most easy to use web server on the planet. A web server of
choice for Web developers (PHP, Ruby, Python, etc) and Web designers.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libmongoose-devel-7.24-1bl1
  libmongoose7.24-7.24-1bl1
  libssl-devel-3.5.9-1
  libssl3-3.5.9-1
  pkg-config-3.0.11-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.13-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  libssl-devel-3.5.9-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/cesanta/mongoose

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/cesanta/mongoose/archive/refs/tags/7.24.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack mongoose-7.24-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./mongoose-7.24-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/mongoose-7.24-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/mongoose-7.24-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libmongoose7.24-7.24-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libmongoose-devel-7.24-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(mongoose)
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/mongoose.README
  /usr/share/doc/mongoose/LICENSE
  /usr/share/doc/mongoose/README.md

(libmongoose7.24)
  /usr/bin/cygmongoose-7-24.dll

(libmongoose-devel)
  /usr/include/mongoose/mongoose.h
  /usr/lib/libmongoose.dll.a
  /usr/lib/pkgconfig/mongoose.pc

